                <pb facs="0361" n="289" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg289"/>

                <head>No. 136.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lowell to Mr. Frelinghuysen</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-08-17"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 17,
                        1882</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>McSweeney has been released without conditions. Slatterly was discharged on the
                    1st of August. The only two remaining cases are those of O’Mahoney and Brophy,
                    and they are being considered by the proper officials.</p>
                <closer><signed>LOWELL,</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
